  "sport": "basketball",
  "title": "Swap partners – pass off the dribble",
  "description": "Players pair up around the half-court line, one ball per pair. The player without the ball runs towards a basket; the player with the ball dribbles after them and passes while still dribbling. The receiver catches at full speed and finishes with a lay-up without stopping.\n\nAfter the finish, both players find a new partner. The shooter grabs the rebound, finds a player without a ball and dribbles towards the other basket. The passer finds a new partner who has a ball and runs towards the other basket to receive. The result is a continuous flow in both directions across the whole court.\n\nProgressions: alternate left- and right-hand lay-ups, pass only one-handed straight off the dribble, or play in silence – eye contact and hands only. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep dribbling until you pass – don't pick the ball up first."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass in front of your partner so they can keep their speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Make eye contact and show your hands before cutting to the basket."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Find a new partner quickly after the finish."
    }
  ],
